ALLOW SSH connections from all IP addresses using the OS firewall and then constrict the SSH connections to your build machine to your particular 
laptop ip address(es) using the GUI system of your cloudhost. This way the OS firewall is a first line of defence and the cloudhost firewall
locks things down so that only particular IP addresses have access to your machine via SSH.
Also, consider only having your build machine "online" when you are actually doing work because an offline machine can't be attacked in other words
shutdown your build machine once you have completed your work and reboot it the next time you have work that you want to do on it.
